/*
  experiments/P7_interface.spthy -- Profile P7 · the INTERFACE lever (ROADMAP #2, first-class interfaces).
  Same VERIFY_KEY phase + sigma6 Abstraction detector as the baseline (cf. P2 / P3 / S0), but the compare
  step is presented via the HARDENED interface (core/interface_hardened_verify.spthy: Effort 'lo'). The
  point: an interface that lowers a step's demand prevents the stressor from firing AT ALL -- upstream of
  the Poka-Yoke mitigations (P6), which block the bad outcome after the stressor fires.

  RFC argument (the proof PAIR): under the BASELINE interface the tampered-key mistake is reachable
  (P2_mistake_reachable, exists-trace); under THIS hardened interface it is unreachable (P7_no_mistake,
  all-traces). Hence the normative requirement: "implementations MUST present the fingerprint comparison
  via a low-Effort affordance (e.g. a side-by-side visual diff), not a raw hex string."
*/

// the ceremony still works: a genuine key is accepted (happy path).
lemma P7_genuine_verify_ok:
  exists-trace
  "Ex p vid #i. Accept(p, vid)@i"

// the hardened interface fires the stressor's PRECONDITION away: sigma6 never onsets.
lemma P7_no_abstraction:
  all-traces
  "not (Ex p #i. Abstraction(p)@i)"

// consequently the Naive mask never arises...
lemma P7_no_naive_verify:
  all-traces
  "not (Ex p vid #i. Verify(p, vid, 'Naive')@i)"

// ...and the tampered-key mistake is UNREACHABLE -- without any outcome-blocking mitigation,
// purely because the better interface kept the user Attentive. (Contrast: P2_mistake_reachable.)
// NB: this profile also poses a set-policy control (below), so P7_no_mistake additionally proves
// no TASK-mediated mistake occurs under the clear control design.
lemma P7_no_mistake:
  all-traces
  "not (Ex p vid #i. Mistake(p, vid)@i)"

// ---- the SAME lever on Pathway B: a CLEAR set-policy control (interface_clear_policy) ----
// the control still works: the safe policy is set (happy path).
lemma P7_clear_policy_safe_reachable:
  exists-trace
  "Ex p pid #i. SetPolicy(p, pid, 'safe')@i"

// ...and the unsafe policy is UNREACHABLE: under honest terminology the task-mediated mistake has
// no cause. Proof pair with P5_misleading_attentive_mistake (misleading seed -> unsafe reachable):
// "the control's options MUST state their effect in plain, unambiguous terms."
lemma P7_no_unsafe_policy:
  all-traces
  "not (Ex p pid #i. SetPolicy(p, pid, 'unsafe')@i)"
